# Seat lock ownership

`RedisService.lockSeat` returns a `SeatHold` when this user acquires the key or already holds it. It returns null when another user holds the key. `SeatHold.release` is the only delete. It removes the key only when the stored value is this user.

Do not add `unlockSeat` back. An unconditional `delete` lets a lost race remove the winner's lock.

In `BookingService.bookSeat`, add a hold to the release list only after `lockSeat` returns it. On failure, release those holds. On success, leave them until the TTL. A second lock by the same user refreshes the TTL. It must not delete the key.

The Redis key uppercases the seat. Pass the catalog spelling from `SeatStatus`, and fold case duplicates before locking.

```java
// BAD — deletes whoever owns the key, including a seat this attempt never locked
redisTemplate.delete("seat-lock:" + eventId + ":" + seatNumber);

// GOOD
RedisService.SeatHold hold = redisService.lockSeat(eventId, seatNumber, userId, 5);
if (hold == null) {
    return failed;
}
holds.add(hold);
```
